# Pairs with MonotonicVisibility. A reshard shadow-forward installs the stale
# prepared write on a leaf that has no record of the saga's terminal - a split
# destination the terminal never reached - rather than on one that already
# applied it. The orphan guard then has nothing to stand on: once the registry
# row has been retired the bucket resolves InFlight, the gate falls through to a
# projection that never received the commit, and a key a reader saw post-saga
# reverts. This is the stranded-prepare class (#2318) at design level, and why
# the action's guard requires the terminal to be present.
MODULE: MonotonicVisibilityOrphanLosesTerminal
TARGET: MonotonicVisibility
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: shadow-forwards an orphan onto a leaf with no record of the terminal, so a committed key reverts once the row is retired
PERTURBS: ShadowForwardOrphan

--- FIND
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![t][k] = "pending"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, vote, decision, terminal, orphanDone, forgotten, masked, revision>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the destination leaf holds no applied terminal for the saga.
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![t][k] = "pending"]
    /\ terminal' = [terminal EXCEPT ![t][k] = "none"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, vote, decision, orphanDone, forgotten, masked, revision>>
--- END
